      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-02-04T22:28:25.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My friends and I aren't hugely experienced, but we're working our way up the adversary levels, one at a time.&nbsp; Haven't lost yet, except for our first game when we had no idea what we were doing.&nbsp; Some have been close, but it's always been by running out the Invader deck.&nbsp; We've never flipped the Blight card, which makes it supposedly a \"dominating victory,\" but when you're on the very last Invader card, it hardly seems that way.&nbsp; I do see that the scoring method does heavily weight invader cards over Blight (2/card remaining vs. 1/(blight /&nbsp;# of players)).</p>\n<p>How about everyone else?&nbsp; Anyone else have the same experience?&nbsp; Or is flipping the Blight card and have everything go to pot from there the more normal path to loss?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:26.014Z",
